# Advisories that currently have no fix, so `npm audit` cannot be made fully clean:
#   - GHSA-g3hv-75wg-m249 (moderate): the minimatch copy bundled inside aws-cdk-lib
#     (10.2.6 in 2.277.0, the latest release), which npm overrides cannot reach.
#     Needs a new aws-cdk-lib release. npm's suggested "fix" is a downgrade to
#     aws-cdk-lib 2.239.0, which is not a real fix.
#   - GHSA-fc5q-39xc-vjpf (high): picomatch <= 4.0.7 has no patched release (4.0.7 is
#     the latest). Dev-only, reached through jest. npm's suggested "fix" (jest 30.2.0)
#     does not remove it. `npm audit` therefore still exits non-zero at the "high" level.
# The gate is set to "high" so that low and moderate findings do not fail the audit.
# Remove the audit-level line (back to the default) once both are fixed upstream.
audit-level=high
